    {
      "tr": "`F.interpolate` dört boyut ister: `t[None, None]` ile `(1, 1, H, W)` yap.",
      "en": "`F.interpolate` needs four dimensions: make `(1, 1, H, W)` with `t[None, None]`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Sonuçtan `[0, 0]` ile iki boyuta dön.",
      "en": "Go back to two dimensions with `[0, 0]`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n**main.py**\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n\ndef upsample_cam(cam, size):\n    t = torch.tensor(cam, dtype=torch.float32)[None, None]\n    big = F.interpolate(t, size=(size, size), mode=\"nearest\")\n    return big[0, 0].tolist()\n\nfor row in upsample_cam([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 2.0]], 4):\n    print(row)\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n**main.py**\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n\ndef upsample_cam(cam, size):\n    t = torch.tensor(cam, dtype=torch.float32)[None, None]\n    big = F.interpolate(t, size=(size, size), mode=\"nearest\")\n    return big[0, 0].tolist()\n\nfor row in upsample_cam([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 2.0]], 4):\n    print(row)\n```"
    }
